{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/stylelintrc.json",

  "//": [
    "T2 from IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md §8 — every rule below is real and tested",
    "(see docs/decisions or the commit history for the verification pass),",
    "not copied from a generic config. Stylelint version matters here: this",
    "was verified against stylelint 17.14.1 specifically — 'color-no-hex' and",
    "similar rules have moved around across major versions before and may",
    "again; re-verify against docs/reference if this config stops matching",
    "reality after an upgrade.",
    "",
    "WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT CATCH (see 'manual checklist' in",
    "IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md §8 for the full list; two CSS-specific gaps",
    "found while building this config, worth naming here):",
    "  - @container value restriction to 700px (E6). Tested empirically:",
    "    media-feature-name-value-allowed-list does NOT apply to @container,",
    "    only @media. No built-in stylelint rule covers this; a custom",
    "    plugin would be needed for one narrow, low-frequency check. Left",
    "    for manual review rather than shipping a fragile custom rule for",
    "    it.",
    "  - text-transform: uppercase used outside a --t-label context. This",
    "    requires knowing which selector corresponds to which type token —",
    "    not a per-declaration value check stylelint can express.",
    "  - Cross-file checks (every var(--x) used is actually defined; light",
    "    and dark token sets have parity; no stray @layer names) are NOT",
    "    stylelint's job — see scripts/verify-tokens.mjs, run separately as",
    "    `pnpm check:tokens`.",
    "  - Cascade LAYER PRIORITY bugs (a correct-looking rule in a",
    "    higher-priority layer silently overriding a more specific rule in a",
    "    lower one — see docs/decisions and the base.css color-scheme",
    "    incident) are a semantic, cross-file cascade issue. No lint rule",
    "    catches this; it was found by testing actual behavior, which is",
    "    the only thing that reliably would."
  ],

  "rules": {
    "color-no-hex": true,
    "color-named": "never",
    "function-disallowed-list": [
      "rgb",
      "rgba",
      "hsl",
      "hsla",
      "hwb",
      "lab",
      "lch",
      "oklab",
      "oklch",
      "color",
      "light-dark"
    ],

    "property-disallowed-list": [
      "box-shadow",
      "-webkit-box-shadow",
      "text-shadow",
      "filter",
      "backdrop-filter"
    ],

    "declaration-property-value-allowed-list": {
      "border-width": ["/^(0|1px|2px|var\\(--bw\\)|var\\(--bw-marker\\))$/"],
      "border-top-width": ["/^(0|1px|2px|var\\(--bw\\)|var\\(--bw-marker\\))$/"],
      "border-right-width": ["/^(0|1px|2px|var\\(--bw\\)|var\\(--bw-marker\\))$/"],
      "border-bottom-width": ["/^(0|1px|2px|var\\(--bw\\)|var\\(--bw-marker\\))$/"],
      "border-left-width": ["/^(0|1px|2px|var\\(--bw\\)|var\\(--bw-marker\\))$/"],

      "border-radius": [
        "/^(0|3px|4px|50%|0 4px 4px 0|var\\(--radius\\)|var\\(--radius-sm\\))$/"
      ],

      "transition-duration": ["/^var\\(--dur(-layout)?\\)$/"],
      "animation-duration": ["/^var\\(--dur(-layout)?\\)$/"],
      "transition-timing-function": ["/^var\\(--ease\\)$/"],
      "animation-timing-function": ["/^var\\(--ease\\)$/"],

      "font-family": ["/^var\\(--font-(serif|sans|mono)\\)$/"],
      "font": ["/^var\\(--t-[a-z0-9-]+\\)$/", "/^inherit$/"],

      "transition-property": [
        "/^(color|background-color|border-color|outline-color|height)$/",
        "/^(color|background-color|border-color|outline-color|height)(,\\s*(color|background-color|border-color|outline-color|height))*$/"
      ]
    },

    "declaration-property-value-disallowed-list": {
      "/^border/": ["/(?<!var\\(--[\\w-]*)\\b(?!0\\b|1px\\b|2px\\b)\\d+(\\.\\d+)?px\\b/"],
      "outline": ["none"]
    },

    "media-feature-name-value-allowed-list": {
      "min-width": ["/^(760px|1280px)$/"]
    }
  },

  "overrides": [
    {
      "//": "tokens.css is the one file allowed to declare literal colours and use light-dark()/oklch() directly — every value in the entire design flows from here.",
      "files": ["src/styles/tokens.css"],
      "rules": {
        "color-no-hex": null,
        "color-named": null,
        "function-disallowed-list": null
      }
    },
    {
      "//": "fonts.css is the one file allowed to write literal font-family names — @font-face is the only place a font's name gets declared in the first place; everywhere else must reference var(--font-*) instead.",
      "files": ["src/styles/fonts.css"],
      "rules": {
        "declaration-property-value-allowed-list": null
      }
    },
    {
      "//": "Astro files need a DIFFERENT parser to extract <style> blocks out of the frontmatter/template structure. Scoped here, not passed as a global --custom-syntax CLI flag — tested and confirmed that applying postcss-html globally makes stylelint silently find ZERO violations in plain .css files (no error, just an empty, wrong result). Real, serious difference: this override touches only .astro files; .css files keep the default CSS parser.",
      "files": ["**/*.astro"],
      "customSyntax": "postcss-html"
    }
  ]
}
